WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.580
This Joker actor may have had a serious case
of jealousy.

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:08.400
According to The Hollywood Reporter, Jared
Leto, who portrayed the Joker in 2016's Suicide

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:13.410
Squad, reportedly attempted to sabotage director
Todd Phillips' standalone Joker movie, which

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:15.320
stars Joaquin Phoenix in the title role.

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:20.460
The outlet cites anonymous sources that claim
Leto was so hurt by and frustrated over the

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:24.669
news that Warner Bros. was moving ahead with
another Joker film that wasn't going to feature

00:00:24.669 --> 00:00:28.890
him as the infamous DC Comics baddie that
he tried to kill the film before it officially

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:29.740
got off the ground.

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:35.219
Insiders with information about the situation
and whom THR claims are, quote, "familiar

00:00:35.219 --> 00:00:39.640
with Leto's behavior" have indicated that
Leto lodged bitter complaints to his agents

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:44.500
at the Creative Artists Agency in Los Angeles
the same company that represents Joker director

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:47.000
Phillips after learning of the rival project.

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:49.400
"I don't want no beef."

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:50.480
"You don't want no beef?

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:52.280
You don't want no beef?

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:53.280
You don't want no beef?"

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:58.719
Leto is said to have asked his agents at CAA
to stop Joker from getting made, allegedly

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:02.760
claiming that the mere existence of the project
was something of a slap in the face.

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:07.430
The actor, who won an Academy Award for his
work in Dallas Buyers Club, reportedly argued

00:01:07.430 --> 00:01:10.440
that, quote, "he wasn't being treated properly
as an Oscar winner."

00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:15.860
Additionally, Leto allegedly asked his music
manager Irving Azoff, an entertainment executive

00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:21.140
who at the time managed Leto's band 30 Seconds
to Mars, to contact, quote, "the leader" of

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:22.680
Warner Bros.' parent company.

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:27.660
It's unclear whether Leto requested Azoff
to call Jeff Bewkes at Time Warner or Randall

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:31.240
Stephenson at AT&amp;T, as both were head honchos
at the time.

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:36.540
Regardless, the alleged reason behind Leto's
inquiry to Azoff was to, quote, "get Warners

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:37.720
to kill the Phillips film."

00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:42.640
It's also been reported that Warner Bros.
executives were "nervous" about Joker, given

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:47.360
its dark tone and gritty, more violent approach
to the namesake comic book character's origin.

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:51.619
The studio gave the project the greenlight
nonetheless, but approved a budget of only

00:01:51.619 --> 00:01:56.979
$55 million a sum that's small in comparison
to other comic book movies and a budget that

00:01:56.979 --> 00:02:01.229
some people at Warner Bros. were reportedly
hoping would frustrate Phillips and cause

00:02:01.229 --> 00:02:03.260
him to abandon the project altogether.

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:05.520
Of course, we know that didn't end up happening.

00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:10.030
A source of Leto's has denied that the actor
ever tried to sabotage the Phoenix-Phillips

00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:14.730
Joker movie, while Azoff, who no longer works
with Leto, declined to provide a comment when

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:16.040
THR reached out.

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:20.440
Word of Jared Leto reportedly trying to kill
the recently released Joker film comes shortly

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:25.170
after The Hollywood Reporter claimed that
the actor was "alienated and upset" upon hearing

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:26.960
the news that the project got the greenlight.

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:31.260
Leto reportedly also felt that Warner Bros.
had been teasing him with the promise of his

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:35.260
own standalone movie, and was hurt that a
different actor received one instead.

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:39.140
Now, it seems that the studio may not have
been serious about putting together a solo

00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:43.830
Joker film starring Leto, as sources close
to the production of Suicide Squad have noted

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:48.580
that Warner Bros. "wasn't thrilled" with Leto's
behavior prior to and during the shooting

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:49.260
of that movie.

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:53.960
Leto took an unorthodox approach to getting
into character for Suicide Squad which included

00:02:53.970 --> 00:02:58.330
sending a live rat to Harley Quinn actress
Margot Robbie, gifting Deadshot actor Will

00:02:58.330 --> 00:03:02.900
Smith a love letter and a bunch of bullets,
and bringing a dead hog to rehearsal.

00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:07.220
His terrifying efforts really weren't worth
it in the end, as Leto's Joker was little

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:09.080
more than a cameo in Suicide Squad.

00:03:09.220 --> 00:03:13.300
Another source has claimed that Leto tried
to, quote, "'invent' a place for himself"

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:16.600
in the film, which was "never really his movie,"
and it all backfired.

00:03:16.990 --> 00:03:21.060
Whatever caused Warner Bros. to back away
from a Leto-led Joker movie and prioritize

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:25.870
Phillips' project instead, we can't say for
certain, but it seems clear that Leto didn't

00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:27.200
like how things played out.

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:32.260
Sadly for Leto, sources have indicated to
THR that the actor's time as the Joker is

00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:33.160
probably over for good.

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:38.070
He isn't included in Birds of Prey which centers
on Joker's ex-flame Harley Quinn, played opposite

00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:42.690
Leto in Suicide Squad by Margot Robbie and
is likely not going to be a part of the upcoming

00:03:42.690 --> 00:03:46.260
Suicide Squad reboot-slash-sequel directed
by James Gunn.

00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:50.030
The filmmaker himself recently said that he
doesn't think it would be strange for Leto's

00:03:50.030 --> 00:03:54.680
Joker to not be in the film, quote, "as he
isn't a part of the Suicide Squad in the comics."

